From f4c3fe6f013fe0f91c4dd2edcdbf7d16937b4546 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wilderness01 <140787484+Wilderness01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 20:15:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iPhone widescreen: Odyssey renders wider (1560x720) on 19.5:9

Upstream-Status: fork-only
Reason: Odyssey renders its own 16:9 picture; the host's DM_SCREEN_ASPECT alone cannot widen it. This adds a wider branch to the host (ratio to 2.2, height fixed) and a FRAME_STEP stub that makes the game's handheld display width follow the host's layout width, so the iPhone 15 Pro Max renders 1560x720 with more scene at the sides instead of black bars or cropping. The present's fallback is the wider layer too: the game's window texture is 1600x900, its crop 1560x720, so the texture's 16:9 does not match the screen's 2.167 and the shape would fall back to 16:9.
Issue: Wilderness01/NX2Apple#1
